# Install the `file:../..` SDK as a real copy instead of a symlink.
#
# A symlinked SDK resolves @strands-agents/sdk from typescript/node_modules
# while this example resolves its own copy, so the same Strands classes exist
# twice — TypeScript then rejects the Agent config (its nominal classes carry
# protected fields) and the runtime loads the framework twice. One resolved
# copy is what lets src/index.ts spread `connectMemoryToAgent`'s result into
# `new Agent({ ... })` with no `as unknown as` casts.
#
# Trade-off: after editing typescript/src you must rebuild the SDK
# (`npm --prefix ../.. run build`) and re-run `npm install` here.
#
# Lockfile caveat: because the SDK is installed as a copy, package-lock.json
# records it inline. The entry MUST keep `"resolved": "file:../.."` — an entry
# without it makes `npm ci` fall back to the *published* @neo4j-labs/agent-memory
# of the same version number, which silently type-checks against a different
# (older) SDK. If `npm ci` ever installs a surface the local `dist/` does not
# have, delete package-lock.json and node_modules and run `npm install`.
install-links=true
